{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://schemas.traigent.ai/analytics/experiment_run_report_response_schema.json",
  "title": "Run Report Canonical Success Response",
  "description": "Platform success envelope for GET /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/experiment-runs/{experiment_run_ref}/report. The report DTO (results/report_payload_response_schema.json) is mirrored under data by a closed definition (not re-used through allOf, because the shared DTO requires the internal trial_id on every row) that declares every field ExperimentReportService.generate_report_payload always emits (src/services/analytics/experiment_report_service.py:279-315: generated_at, experiment_context, methodology, example_index_map, provenance, aggregated_results, raw_example_results, insights, warnings), each bounded in shape. CANONICAL PROJECTION OMITS INTERNAL IDS (internal ids never appear in payloads): the canonical projection omits experiment_context.experiment_id: internal id; omits experiment_context.run_id: internal id; omits provenance.source_endpoints: its URLs embed the internal run id; omits report_id: it embeds the internal run id (report_<run_id>_<hash>, experiment_report_service.py:264). The closed branch rejects these properties. data.provenance.run_id is REQUIRED and is the experiment_run_ref (^experiment_run_[0-9a-f]{32}$); the canonical projection populates it from the resolved reference (backend obligation), never from the historical run id. trial_ref (an opaque persisted reference) and example_id are the row identity; trial_id is omitted (internal configuration-run id). config_params follows the sanitizer shapes (src/services/analytics/config_redaction.py:79-82, :111-172): nesting to depth 3, lists of at most 12 items, strings of at most 128 characters, at most 64 keys per object; empty objects and arrays are accepted at the depth limit, as the sanitizer emits them. Row identity is the opaque run-scoped trial_ref (^(trial_[0-9a-f]{16}|configuration_run_[0-9a-f]{32})$, defined once in experiment_run_trial_ref_schema.json: The configuration run's issued public reference (configuration_runs.configuration_run_ref; backend infrastructure/migrations/versions/20261122_0001_configuration_run_ref_role_v1.py:1-24: sessions issue trial_ plus 16 hex, an issued reference is never re-minted, UNIQUE (tenant_id, configuration_run_ref), NULL until the reference backfill). Two issued formats exist: trial_ plus 16 hex (issued by sessions; backend src/dal/configuration_run_dal.py:50) and configuration_run_ plus 32 hex (minted by mint_configuration_run_ref, configuration_run_dal.py:60, :345, called from src/services/configuration_run_service.py:238). Issued once, never re-minted, so it is stable across views, pages and deletion of other configurations. The internal id is never emitted. A canonical view of a run with any configuration whose reference is not yet issued is the closed 503 until the backfill completes (never a positional or synthetic stand-in). Shared by aggregate and example rows); trial_id (the internal configuration-run id, builder :1621-1629, :1707) is rejected. The projection must also scrub internal ids embedded in warnings, insight evidence and fallback config labels (backend obligation; builder :1621-1629, :1707, :1777, :1887-1891, :1933, :2288). SIZE: this schema gives NO static byte bound. The 8 MiB limit (x-max-response-bytes 8388608) is enforced on the serialized envelope: the handler measures the final serialized bytes, sends those same bytes, and returns the closed 503 when over the limit. Collection caps are realistic limits (aggregated_results 1000, raw_example_results 5000 with example_index_map the same displayed rows, insights 50 computed over the full population, warnings 1000 of at most 512 characters). Rows beyond a cap are truncated server-side, deterministically; meta.aggregated_results_total and meta.raw_example_results_total (required integers) carry the untruncated counts. meta and metadata are bounded maps of strings, booleans, null and safe-range integers. The historical envelope run_report_response_schema.json is unchanged and still serves the deprecated analytics path. The optimization report payload (report.get_optimization_report_payload, W8) is a different contract and is not merged here.",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "x-max-response-bytes": 8388608,
